{"agent":"impl-od","data":{"body":"Entry: id, what, why, since, default, answer command, blocks (items transitively, from the item graph), owner, severity escalating with age ([digest].escalate_after). Order: severity, impact, age. Replay test: fold the real log of a week, assert counts sane. Folds AW-inbox (proposed). Conformance: every threshold is a knob settable by file, CLI, MCP and prompt (D-everything-configurable); no new MCP tool (D-mcp-new-nouns); reuse the shared engines; files under 20 KB; deterministic (same state and now, same text); research docs/ddflow/research/operator-digest.md, proposal docs/ddflow/decisions/operator-digest.md.\n\nFolded AW-inbox (ddflow inbox: everything waiting on the operator, in one list): D-OD-Q4: operator accepted the fold 2026-10-23.\n\nOne read-only list of what only a person can do or decide: items in the 'questions' state (e.g. DX-waves-status) with the question text, proposed (unaccepted) decisions, chore approvals pending (ddflow chore approve is a person's act), bugs or completions that need an override the hook forbids to agents (fix-Bci-ruff-check..., RM-tool-diet-research, B998bcca9ce style), unavailable-reviewer escalations, contested decisions, gates recorded partial/forced awaiting spot-check (ddflow gate list --refuted), expired credentials or quota pauses. Each row: what, since when, who is waiting on it, the exact command to answer it. CLI + MCP, --json, exit 0 even if non-empty (an inbox is not a failure). Also shown as a line in brief and status ('3 items wait for you'). Conformance: every threshold is a knob settable by file, CLI, MCP and prompt (D-everything-configurable); declare new commands with family and action (D-mcp-tool-families); reuse the shared engines; files under 20 KB; no private addresses or keys in tracked files or in any message sent.","globs":["ddflow/services/digest/queue.py","ddflow/config_sections/digest.py","ddflow/config.py","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.digest.*.t